  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-06-23T19:33:04.443Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If the world is PC only (example: The Great Pug), use local IK exclusively. Else if the world is cross-platform (example: The Great Pug - West) or Quest only (example: Quest Only Club), use networked IK exclusively.\n\nThis way PC users can make use of the much more accurate local IK with the vastly more powerful CPUs than the Quest, which with this implementation would be completely spared from the computational load of local IK. In addition, it will reduce network traffic since the majority of players play on PC only worlds, therefore networked IK will function better than in current iterations (Build 801 for instance)",
